description:
A weather API is reached through an interface, so the logic around it can be tested without a network:

```csharp
public record Forecast(string City, double TempC, string Summary);

public interface IWeatherApi
{
    Task<Forecast> GetAsync(string city, CancellationToken ct = default);   // throws HttpRequestException on failure
}

public class WeatherService(IWeatherApi api, Func<DateTime> clock)
{
    public async Task<string> DescribeAsync(string city, CancellationToken ct = default)
}
```

`DescribeAsync` returns `"<City>: <TempC with 1 decimal> C, <Summary>"` (invariant culture), and:
- **trims** the city name and treats it case-insensitively; a blank name throws `ArgumentException` before any call;
- **caches** results per city for 10 minutes, measured with `clock()` (so the tests can move time forward);
- **retries** an `HttpRequestException` whose `StatusCode` is null, 429 or 500 and above, up to 3 attempts in total, waiting 10 ms then 20 ms; other errors (such as 404) are not retried;
- when every attempt fails but a cached result exists (even an old one), returns that result with ` (cached)` added; otherwise lets the last exception through.

